<title>INDIA: CRICKET - NEW ZEALAND 285-7 INNINGS CLOSED V PAKISTAN.</title>
<headline>CRICKET - NEW ZEALAND 285-7 INNINGS CLOSED V PAKISTAN.</headline>
<dateline>MOHALI, India 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand scored 285 for the loss of seven wickets in their 50 overs in the opening match against Pakistan in the four-nation Independence Cup cricket tournament on Friday.</p>
<p>Pakistan</p>
<p> S.Anwar c Harris b Penn	    17</p>
<p> S.Afridi b Larsen		    59</p>
<p> R.Raja run out			 11</p>
<p> I.Ahmed lbw b Astle		  50</p>
<p> S.Malik c Harris b Astle	   47</p>
<p> Inzaman-ul-Haq c Harris b Patel  30</p>
<p> M.Khan c Fleming b Astle	   16</p>
<p> M.Hussain c Davis b Larsen	  1</p>
<p> A.Razzak st Parore b Astle	  8</p>
<p> S.Mushtaq not out		     6</p>
<p> Aaqib Javed not out		   6</p>
<p> Extras (lb-2 nb-3 w-7)	     12</p>
<p> Total (for 9 wickets, 50 overs) 263</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-45 2-92 3-106 4-187 5-220 6-232 7-242</p>
<p>8-243 9-256.</p>
<p>Bowling: Penn 6-0-50-1 (3w), Davis 6-0-39-0 (4w, 2nb),</p>
<p>Harris 10-2-34-0, Larsen 10-0-46-2 (1nb), Patel 10-0-49-1, Astle</p>
<p>8-0-43-4.</p>
<p>Result: New Zealand won by 22 runs.</p>
</text>
